---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — realfileeditor"
  description="How realfileeditor handles your files and data: what's processed in your browser, what's deleted automatically, and what analytics we collect."
  path="/privacy-policy"
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--accent)] mb-3">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--fg-muted)] mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-[var(--fg-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--fg)] font-semibold mb-2">Your files</h2>
        <p>
          The tools on realfileeditor (compress, merge, split, rotate, watermark, convert, zip) process
          your files directly in your browser using JavaScript. In the current version of the site, files
          are not uploaded to our servers to perform these operations — they never leave your device
          during processing. If a future version of a tool requires server-side processing, that will be
          stated clearly on the tool's page before you use it, and any uploaded file will be deleted
          automatically on the schedule you choose (as low as 30 minutes).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--fg)] font-semibold mb-2">Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics to understand which tools and pages are used, so we can prioritize what
          to build next. Google Analytics uses cookies and may collect information such as your
          approximate location, device type, and browsing behavior on this site. It does not have access
          to the contents of files you process. You can opt out using your browser's cookie settings or a
          browser extension such as Google's Analytics Opt-out Add-on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--fg)] font-semibold mb-2">Cookies &amp; local storage</h2>
        <p>
          We use your browser's local storage to remember preferences like light/dark mode and your
          chosen language. These stay on your device and are not sent to us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--fg)] font-semibold mb-2">Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which may log requests including your IP address, per
          Google's own privacy policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--fg)] font-semibold mb-2">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We'll update this page if how we handle data changes, and update the "last updated" date above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg text-[var(--fg)] font-semibold mb-2">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can go to
          <a href="mailto:anshumanverma756@gmail.com" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline">anshumanverma756@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
